From: George Xu <george.xu@slack-corp.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 21:16:10 -0700
Subject: feat: use the macOS native picker only for picker-issued capture ids

Electron opens Chromium's NativeScreenCapturePickerMac for
session.setDisplayMediaRequestHandler's useSystemPicker option through
content::desktop_capture::OpenNativeScreenCapturePicker.

Upstream only creates the picker when kUseSCContentSharingPicker is on,
and that feature also assumes every macOS desktop capture belongs to the
picker: getSources() thumbnails switch to DelegatedSourceListCapturer, any
id the picker did not issue fails with "missing authorized filter", and
stopping any capture device closes the picker session with the same id.
Electron apps still capture getSources() ids through getDisplayMedia() and
the legacy chromeMediaSource: 'desktop' constraint, so the feature can't
be turned on.

Instead, always create the picker on macOS, and only hand ids tagged
IdType::kNativePickerSession (serialized with a ":s" suffix) to it, both
when starting a capture device and when closing one. Every other id keeps
the regular ScreenCaptureKit path. Chrome's own picker flow always tags
its ids, so its behavior is unchanged; ids it did not issue now capture
normally instead of failing, which would be the argument for upstreaming.

diff --git a/content/browser/media/capture/native_screen_capture_picker.cc b/content/browser/media/capture/native_screen_capture_picker.cc
index 152f3aa78032ee3f8c48fbefe052a2f1d85bed6b..c9155f67d1c78bbc17b64fdeb4c7775dc7c4d254 100644
--- a/content/browser/media/capture/native_screen_capture_picker.cc
+++ b/content/browser/media/capture/native_screen_capture_picker.cc
@@ -6,7 +6,6 @@
 
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC)
 #include "content/browser/media/capture/native_screen_capture_picker_mac.h"
-#include "media/base/media_switches.h"
 #endif
 
 namespace content {
@@ -14,11 +13,10 @@ namespace content {
 std::unique_ptr<NativeScreenCapturePicker>
 MaybeCreateNativeScreenCapturePicker() {
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC)
-  if (base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(media::kUseSCContentSharingPicker)) {
-    return CreateNativeScreenCapturePickerMac();
-  }
-#endif
+  return CreateNativeScreenCapturePickerMac();
+#else
   return nullptr;
+#endif
 }
 
 }  // namespace content
